# LiveKit (platform default; per-account overrides live in meeting_provider_config)
#
# Points at the LIVE SFU on purpose — local dev does NOT run its own LiveKit
# container any more. The local stack advertised the laptop's LAN IP in its ICE
# candidates, so every DHCP change silently broke media and needed
# infra/set-node-ip.sh + a compose restart. Using the live server removes that
# whole class of failure: its IP is stable.
#
# Consequence: the local `turaquant-livekit-1` / `-egress-1` containers are now
# unused. Stop them with
#   docker compose stop livekit egress
# (TuraClickMeet's separate stack on 7880-7882 is untouched.)
LIVEKIT_URL=wss://livekit.turaquant.turacoz.com
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=API9e974731b257
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=QObizA5m0lAExQr9aO6eHm_jo89l0FjFddHXEO3O2V-8ItOdQUq04A

# MUST stay non-empty locally. Shares one LiveKit server with production, so an
# empty prefix means local meeting 14 and the live board's meeting 14 are the
# same room. See app/core/config.py.
LIVEKIT_ROOM_PREFIX=dev-

# Base URL used to build every link we EMAIL out — the participant's meeting
# join link and the client's portal link. Deliberately the LIVE domain even on a
# laptop: an emailed http://localhost:3000 link is useless to the person who
# receives it, and the default was exactly that.
# To test a link locally, paste its /meeting/join/... or /client/... path onto
# localhost:3000 by hand rather than changing this.
APP_PUBLIC_URL=https://turaquant.turacoz.com
